From 999f2a06e9f63ea2a8ae9d89e0f2f2ebe3078a64 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Wiklander <jenswi@kernel.org>
Date: Thu, 25 Jun 2026 17:03:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 848/913] ta: pkcs11: fix stack buffer overflow in
 unwrap_rsa_aes_key

When TEE_AsymmetricDecrypt() returns TEE_ERROR_SHORT_BUFFER, it
updates the aes_key_size variable to the required larger size.
Using this updated variable during the cleanup path causes
TEE_MemFill() to overflow the local stack buffer.

Fix this by using sizeof(aes_key_value) to ensure the memory
wipe is strictly bounded to the allocated array size.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/optee_os.git f24f2abcdb1be300e8bceebdbaa75aedf370a737 ta: pkcs11: fix stack buffer overflow in unwrap_rsa_aes_key]
Fixes: 45d40bda652a ("ta: pkcs11: Add RSA AES key wrap")
Change-Id: Id39fd5cfcf84338e795d062d53076e31204c4a41
Signed-off-by: Jens Wiklander <jenswi@kernel.org>
Reviewed-by: Etienne Carriere <etienne.carriere@st.com>
(cherry picked from commit 9bcaec96ede2c8278137939d0dbad3dca887a502)
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/optee/optee_os/+/609430
ACI: CITOOLS <MDG-smet-aci-reviews@list.st.com>
Reviewed-by: Yann GAUTIER <yann.gautier@foss.st.com>
Domain-Review: Yann GAUTIER <yann.gautier@foss.st.com>
Tested-by: Yann GAUTIER <yann.gautier@foss.st.com>
ACI: CIBUILD <MDG-smet-aci-builds@list.st.com>
Reviewed-by: Thomas BOURGOIN <thomas.bourgoin@foss.st.com>
---
 ta/pkcs11/src/processing_asymm.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/ta/pkcs11/src/processing_asymm.c b/ta/pkcs11/src/processing_asymm.c
index 2f59922b0..ea0b6918b 100644
--- a/ta/pkcs11/src/processing_asymm.c
+++ b/ta/pkcs11/src/processing_asymm.c
@@ -1227,7 +1227,7 @@ static enum pkcs11_rc unwrap_rsa_aes_key(struct active_processing *proc,
 
 	*out_sz = target_key_size;
 out:
-	TEE_MemFill(aes_key_value, 0, aes_key_size);
+	TEE_MemFill(aes_key_value, 0, sizeof(aes_key_value));
 	mbedtls_nist_kw_free(&kw_ctx);
 	return rc;
 }
